<title>KUWAIT: Kuwait bank assets rise 0.8 pct in June.</title>
<headline>Kuwait bank assets rise 0.8 pct in June.</headline>
<dateline>KUWAIT 1996-09-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Combined assets of Kuwaiti banks rose 0.8 percent to 11.194 billion dinars at the end of June from 11.106 billion at the end of May, the Central Bank's monthly bulletin said.</p>
<p>Assets were 11.765 billion dinars in June 1995.</p>
<p>			Figures in million Kuwaiti dinars</p>
<p>					     June '96	  June '95</p>
<p> Cash					  48.9		 56.7</p>
<p> Balances with Central Bank	    50.1		 93.0</p>
<p> Public debt instruments	     1898.4	     1931.9</p>
<p> Debt purchase bonds		   3142.1	     3736.1</p>
<p> Other					 --		    0.2</p>
<p> Other local investments		296.0		271.9</p>
<p>Credit facilities to</p>
<p>  residents				2740.7	     2112.8</p>
<p> Foreign assets			  2032.8	     1991.4</p>
<p> Inter bank local deposits	    506.1		737.9</p>
<p> Other assets			     478.9		832.6</p>
<p> Total				    11194.2	    11764.7</p>
<p>Note. Data covers eight commercial and specialised banks, the Islamic institution Kuwait Finance House and a Kuwaiti branch of a Bahrain-based bank.</p>
<p>Debt purchase bonds include the value of the purchase by the government of the real estate portfolio of Kuwait Finance House in December 1992.</p>
<p>Slight discrepancies in totals are due to rounding.</p>
<p>($1 = 0.2999 dinars)</p>
<p>-- Inal Ersan, Kuwait newsroom +965-243-1920</p>
